<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Buzurg Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Buzurg Khan Khoja</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Buzurg Khan was a Khoja of the Afaqi line, descended from the former rulers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashgar">Kashgar</a>, who lived in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kokand">Kokand</a>. In 1865 rebels in Kashgar invited him to lead them against Qing rule, and he arrived with the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaqub-beg">Yaqub Beg</a>. Yaqub Beg soon sidelined him and built his own state, Yettishar, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarim-basin">Tarim Basin</a>.</p></div>
